        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ben Gibbard, Jimmy Tamborello, Jenny Lewis, Matthew Brue, David Butler\n- Bands: The Postal Service, Death Cab for Cutie, Dntel, Headset, Rilo Kiley, Missio\n- Songs: We Will Become Silhouettes\n- Companies: Sub Pop Records\n- Places: Seattle, Washington\n\nFacts:\n- The Postal Service were an American indie rock band from Seattle, Washington.\n- The Postal Service consisted of vocalist Ben Gibbard, who was of Death Cab for Cutie, and producer Jimmy Tamborello, who was of Dntel and Headset, with Jenny Lewis of Rilo Kiley on background vocals.\n- \"We Will Become Silhouettes\" is a single by the American indie band The Postal Service.\n- \"We Will Become Silhouettes\" was released on February 8, 2005, under the Sub Pop Records label.\n- Missio currently consists of founding member Matthew Brue, who is a vocalist and producer, and David Butler, who is a producer and instrumentalist.",
